<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Defenestration of Prague (1618)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1618">1618</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Second Defenestration of Prague · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Defenestration of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> took place on 23 May 1618, when Protestant nobles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, angered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> restrictions on their religious rights, threw two Catholic regents and their secretary from a window of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague-castle">Prague Castle</a>. All three survived the fall. The act began the Bohemian Revolt against the Habsburgs, which grew into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/defenestration-of-prague-1618.jpg" alt="Defenestration of Prague (1618)" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prager_Fenstersturz_Wahrhafftige_Zeitung_aus_Prag.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
